[
  {
    "name": "Built-in widgets",
    "description": "Every built-in widget on its own tab, plus a Grouping tab showing two Parameter echo cards sharing a Ticker group. Nothing here needs a backend, a key or a sign-up -- it opens and works the moment you import it.",
    "img": "/openbq/bdobb-logo.svg",
    "img_dark": "data:image/svg+xml;base64,",
    "img_light": "data:image/svg+xml;base64,",
    "allowCustomization": true,
    "tabs": {
      "note": {
        "id": "note",
        "name": "Note",
        "layout": [
          {
            "i": "note",
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "w": 20,
            "h": 10,
            "state": {
              "params": {
                "text": "This is a Note card. Its text is a hidden parameter, so it does not clutter the header's controls row and it travels with the dashboard on export. Click anywhere in the body to edit; Escape throws a draft away."
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "markdown": {
        "id": "markdown",
        "name": "Markdown",
        "layout": [
          {
            "i": "markdown",
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "w": 26,
            "h": 16,
            "state": {
              "params": {
                "text": "# Markdown card\n\nA rich-text note with a formatting toolbar. Edits save on their own about half a second after you stop typing.\n\n## What it can show\n\n- Headings, like the two above\n- A bulleted list, like this one\n- **Bold**, *italic*, and a [link to the Workspace docs](https://docs.openbb.co/workspace)\n\n```\nconst example = \"a fenced code block\";\n```\n"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "clock": {
        "id": "clock",
        "name": "Clock",
        "layout": [
          {
            "i": "clock",
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "w": 18,
            "h": 16,
            "state": {
              "params": {
                "zones": "America/New_York,Europe/London,Asia/Tokyo",
                "layout": "vertical",
                "hourCycle": "24",
                "face": "dots"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "i": "clock",
            "x": 18,
            "y": 0,
            "w": 22,
            "h": 8,
            "state": {
              "params": {
                "zones": "America/New_York,Europe/London,Asia/Tokyo",
                "layout": "horizontal",
                "hourCycle": "24",
                "face": "dots"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "website": {
        "id": "website",
        "name": "Website",
        "layout": [
          {
            "i": "website",
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "w": 40,
            "h": 24,
            "state": {
              "params": {
                "url": "https://docs.openbb.co/workspace"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "rss": {
        "id": "rss",
        "name": "RSS",
        "layout": [
          {
            "i": "rss",
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "w": 22,
            "h": 20,
            "state": {
              "params": {
                "url": "https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/business/rss.xml",
                "limit": "20"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "grouping": {
        "id": "grouping",
        "name": "Grouping",
        "layout": [
          {
            "i": "note",
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "w": 20,
            "h": 8,
            "state": {
              "params": {
                "text": "The two Parameter echo cards below share a Ticker group: the chain-link beside each card's Ticker control opens the Groups menu, the numbered badge shows which group a control is in, and editing either card's Ticker moves both."
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "i": "param_echo",
            "x": 0,
            "y": 8,
            "w": 14,
            "h": 6,
            "groups": [
              "Ticker"
            ],
            "state": {
              "params": {
                "date": "$currentDate"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "i": "param_echo",
            "x": 14,
            "y": 8,
            "w": 14,
            "h": 6,
            "groups": [
              "Ticker"
            ],
            "state": {
              "params": {
                "date": "$currentDate"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "groups": [
      {
        "name": "Ticker",
        "type": "param",
        "paramName": "ticker",
        "defaultValue": "AAPL"
      }
    ],
    "prompts": []
  },
  {
    "name": "Demo providers",
    "description": "One card per provider that answers on the openbq-docker v3 stack (Adventures-OpenBQ/openbq-docker v3.0.0) with no sign-up. Keyless: BLS, CFTC, EconDB, Nasdaq (historical EPS for IBM, in place of the Alpha Vantage card of earlier releases) and the Video Library. EIA and Congress.gov run on the public demo keys in openbq-docker's committed credentials.demo.env, which the stack uses when there is no credentials.env; your own keys in credentials.env take their place. Widget ids are openbq-docker's, checked 2026-10-14 against its /widgets.json as captured by BDOBB's v6 regression run; the EconDB and Video Library (openbb-videos) cards are the extensions openbq-docker v3 adds. EconDB answers under openbb-core 2's provider-prefixed id econdb_economy_indicators_econdb_obb (the ODP 4 id economy_indicators_econdb_obb came from a shared economy router openbq-docker does not install), and its Indicators route needs a country as well as a symbol: RGDP for US, since symbol=RGDP alone is a 422. The BLS card uses bls_search (category=cpi, query=CUUR0000SA0), not bls_series: BLS's own HTTP API needs no key for either fetcher, but openbb-bls's BlsSeriesFetcher never overrides the base Fetcher class's require_credentials=True the way BlsSearchFetcher does, so bls_series 400s on a blank BLS_API_KEY -- bls_search answers 200 with real data on first import, which is the point of this dashboard.",
    "img": "/openbq/bdobb-logo.svg",
    "img_dark": "data:image/svg+xml;base64,",
    "img_light": "data:image/svg+xml;base64,",
    "allowCustomization": true,
    "tabs": {
      "demo-providers": {
        "id": "demo-providers",
        "name": "Demo providers",
        "layout": [
          {
            "i": "eia_short_term_energy_outlook_eia_obb",
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "w": 20,
            "h": 12,
            "state": {
              "params": {}
            }
          },
          {
            "i": "uscongress_bills_congress_gov_obb",
            "x": 20,
            "y": 0,
            "w": 20,
            "h": 12,
            "state": {
              "params": {
                "congress": "119"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "i": "bls_search_bls_obb",
            "x": 0,
            "y": 12,
            "w": 20,
            "h": 12,
            "state": {
              "params": {
                "category": "cpi",
                "query": "CUUR0000SA0"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "i": "cftc_cot_cftc_obb",
            "x": 20,
            "y": 12,
            "w": 20,
            "h": 12,
            "state": {
              "params": {}
